# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
# Cloudflare Pages renders single-page applications natively: when the build
# output contains no top-level 404.html (this project has none), any path that
# does not match a static asset (/, /login, /dashboard, /trains, /analytics, ...)
# is served index.html with a 200, so React Router handles the route on a direct
# visit or a browser refresh. Real static assets are always matched first.
#
# Do NOT add a catch-all rule such as `/* /index.html 200` here: Cloudflare
# rejects it with "Infinite loop detected in this rule" (code 100324), because
# the destination /index.html is normalized (strip .html, then /index -> /) back
# into a path that `/*` itself matches, which re-triggers the rule forever.
# No secret is ever placed in a Cloudflare environment variable - AI provider
# credentials (GEMINI_API_KEY) belong to the Render backend only.
